<p><br />
<br />
Thank you so much for your interest in sponsoring &nbsp;blood drives through the American Red Cross! Sponsoring a Blood Drive is a gift for both the sponsor and the blood recipients, and&nbsp;we are so thankful for your commitment to saving lives through blood donation, especially during this time of Critical&nbsp;Need.</p>

<p>To get started, please look at the two attachments. The first one is our Blood Drive Sign Up sheet. This is to determine what sort of interest you have at your location for donating, and it will help us decide on a goal for your drive.You can start asking people now if they would be willing to give blood at your drive, even though we haven&#39;t set a date yet. The second attachment is our Successful Blood Drive Guide. This is a simplified, step-by-step guide for success, and it will give you an overview of what a sponsor needs to do to host a drive.</p>

<p>Once we determine the interest level, either your area Account Manager&nbsp;or I would need to come out to your location to view where you&nbsp;would be holding the drive to do a site check, as well as to give you some additional information about sponsoring a blood drive. I would only need about thirty&nbsp;minutes of your time. I will be in touch with you in a few days to see what sort of interest you have, and then we can proceed with looking at dates.<br />
<br />
As a sponsor, your main job is to recruit donors from your location to donate. All of the other details will be worked out, but if you and your team can communicate your enthusiasm for the drive and bring donors to the table, you will be a success! .<br />
<br />
Thank you so much for your commitment to saving lives through blood donation!</p>
